{
  "description": "Gems (docs/draft/gem-system.md). Generated at --migrate into items: gem-<type>-<size>-uncut, gem-<type>-<size>-<quality>, and ring-/necklace-<type>-<size>-<quality>. A natural type (pearls) has no rough form: it is found with its quality and never rolls from kills or rock. A gem's value is base_value x the size multiplier (x the quality multiplier once cut); its rarity follows the value. Curves are [x, value] points, interpolated log-linearly between points and held flat past the ends. type_tilt and size_tilt reweight the type and size rolls: weight = drop_rate x tilt ^ log10(base_value / 1000) for types, and drop_rate x tilt ^ log10(multiplier) for sizes. A tilt of 1 leaves the base drop_rates alone; below 1 favours cheap/small gems, above 1 valuable/large ones.",
